plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? Melissa and LoveLetter made use of the trust that exists between friends or colleagues. Imagine receiving an}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ? (71) \uc1 \u160 ? }{\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 from a friend who asks you to open it. This is what happens with Melissa and several other similar email}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ? (72) \uc1 \u160 ? }{\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 . Upon running, such worms usually proceed to send themselves out to email addresses from the victim's address book, previous emails, web pages}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ? (73) \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? As administrators seek to block dangerous email attachments through the recognition of well-known}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ? (74) \uc1 \u160 ? }{\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 , virus writers use other extensions to circumvent such protection. Executable (.exe) files are renamed to .bat and .cmd plus a whole list of other extensions and will still nm and successfully infect target users.}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?Frequently, hackers try to penetrate networks by sending an attachment that looks like a flash movie, which, while displaying some cute animation, simultaneously runs commands in the background to steal your passwords and give the}{\fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ? (75) \uc1 \u160 ? }{\b1 \fs28 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 access to your network.}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 71}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \dbch \f6 {\uc1 \u12289 ?}A. attachment \uc1 \u160 ?B. packet \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C. datagram \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? D. message}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 72}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \dbch \f6 {\uc1 \u12289 ?}A. virtual \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?B. virus \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? C. worms \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? D. bacteria}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 73}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \dbch \f6 {\uc1 \u12289 ?}A. memory \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? B. caches \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C. ports \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?D. registers}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hi